= Using the inidom class =

The [../classes/html/classinidom.html inidom] class provides a framework for DOM parsing of INI-formatted data.  It parses a file or string of INI-formatted data and produces a dom tree representing the data.  Since the inidom class creates a representation of the INI data in memory, it should not be used to process arbitrarily large files which could exhaust system memory.

The dom tree uses "s" elements for sections, "k" elements for keys, "p" elements for pound-delimited comments, and "c" elements for semicolon-delimited comments.  Each element has a "v" attribute containing the value.  Each "k" element also has a "k" attribute containing the key name.

The following program parses an INI string containing a list of animals organized into sections, walks the tree to print each animal's properties, and writes the INI data back to standard output.

